# Verdicts
V1 with ONLY measured levers (8x split + widened delete), the kick cost required to fit
   4 cores at 10^9 rtf 100 is 23 us = 472x the floor: the 42-56 ns floor is
   NOT on the 10^9 critical path (kick cost and cadence are redundant levers).
V2 at the floor, even shipped cadence fits: 0.17 cores.
V3 the graded encounter levers leave 62-571 cores (277d's own composition; recomputed here
   69-586 from the cube base x 14-24x): the one CPU term whose closing
   lever (routing) is ungraded.
V4 memory: only the measured phase-locked program class (21-40 bits) fits 6 GB; every generic
   floor busts it; the shipped plateau is 808x the whole budget.

